{#
  Dream sequence injection.
  When the player rests, sleeps, or is unconscious, the narrator
  can weave in visions drawn from distant events in the shared world.

  The dreams are deliberately cryptic — the player gets fragmentary
  impressions of what other players are doing, filtered through
  symbolism and atmosphere.
#}

{% set dreams = getDreamVisions() %}
{% if dreams and dreams.length > 0 %}
<dreamContent>
The character's sleep is restless. Fragmentary visions surface from the shared world-dream:
{% for vision in dreams %}
  <vision>{{ vision }}</vision>
{% endfor %}
If narrating a rest/sleep scene, you MAY weave ONE of these visions into a brief, atmospheric dream sequence. Present it as a dream — disjointed, symbolic, unsettling or beautiful. The character wakes uncertain whether it meant anything. Do NOT explain the vision or make it literal. Do NOT use more than 2-3 sentences for the dream.
</dreamContent>
{% endif %}
